Investigate a solid chemical's composition, physical condition and supply (@cs-solid-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Storage-Handling-and-Transport-Solid-Fertilizers.lingua#r_7QADF65GMMER3S52G9ANCVR2G8", #source "../sources/Emissions-from-Storage-BREF.lingua#r_4QFPS62AY03WVQB72BMNJQGC43", #source "../sources/Validation-Including-Sampling-Eurachem.lingua#r_0H2SA2SC85XXDYT629N3E3KGXA", #source "../../../../stem/chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Ammonia-Acids-Fertilisers-BREF.lingua#r_45NWBJYAMXXSRV071A57EM02GB", #chemical-supply-systems "A-complete-qualified-chemical-supply-system.lingua#r_44MR9J6NH9MF50YCHKGAT4GMK3") { r_4XZ70HP009HDGSE7NRWJ38BXPN
**Read:** [Storage, handling and transportation of solid mineral fertilizers — Fertilizers Europe](../sources/Storage-Handling-and-Transport-Solid-Fertilizers.lingua#r_7QADF65GMMER3S52G9ANCVR2G8), the entire guide and applicable primary references; [Emissions from Storage — European Commission BREF](../sources/Emissions-from-Storage-BREF.lingua#r_4QFPS62AY03WVQB72BMNJQGC43), complete solid-storage/transfer and emission chapters; [Validation of Measurement Procedures that Include Sampling — Eurachem](../sources/Validation-Including-Sampling-Eurachem.lingua#r_0H2SA2SC85XXDYT629N3E3KGXA), the whole guide and relevant sampling methods; [Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers, BREF LVIC-AAF](../../../../stem/chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Ammonia-Acids-Fertilisers-BREF.lingua#r_45NWBJYAMXXSRV071A57EM02GB), complete relevant production/feed chapters.

Choose a granular fertiliser, salt or powdered industrial feed with a documented user requirement. Read the whole industry handling guide and relevant complete EFS, manufacturing and sampling methods. Characterise the actual quantity/nutrient/active-content basis, composition, moisture, particle distribution and handling state.

Trace an entire chain through production, dispatch, storage, transfers and use. Develop a representative-sampling argument and distinguish average composition from the distribution experienced by a user. Examine segregation, attrition, moisture change, caking and contact contamination using actual data/methods or explicitly labelled hypotheses.

Compare packaged and bulk arrangements on usable quality, accessible capacity, logistics, work, environmental pathways and total service. Build a complete mass/constituent and package account, a replenishment/state model and at least three interruption/change cases. Evaluate alternatives on the same intended-use requirement rather than on tonnes delivered alone.

Use complete primary methods for any property measurement or equipment-design claim. Where physical work is possible, preserve the actual sample and operating history; otherwise report a public-case or supplied-data reconstruction and its unresolved physical tests. Defend the study through derivations, independent numerical checks, competing interpretations and revision. Extend its research question into a full scholarly investigation rather than ending at a list of storage recommendations.

**Continue:** [Defend one complete chemical supply from origin to use and recovery](A-complete-qualified-chemical-supply-system.lingua#r_44MR9J6NH9MF50YCHKGAT4GMK3).

